    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Venezuela left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombia in 1830 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-antonio-paez">José Antonio Páez</a> and for a century was ruled mainly by caudillos.</li><li>Oil found in the 1910s and 1920s made it a leading exporter, a founder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/opec">OPEC</a> and a stable democracy after 1958.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugo-chavez">Hugo Chávez</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicolas-maduro">Nicolás Maduro</a> it became the Bolivarian Republic, then suffered economic collapse and mass emigration.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Venezuela has the world’s largest proven oil reserves, estimated at around 300 billion barrels, mostly heavy crude in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orinoco-belt">Orinoco Belt</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

